<doctext field_name="doctext">Looks like you want a Negative Lookbehind Assertion:&lt;P&gt;

&lt;I&gt;(?&lt;!foo)	Negative Lookbehind	Asserts that what immediately precedes the current position in the string is not foo&lt;/I&gt;&lt;P&gt;

&lt;H5&gt; update&lt;/H5&gt;&lt;P&gt;

maybe try &lt;C&gt;s/(?&lt;!\bisn)(?&lt;!\baren)'t/ 't/g&lt;/C&gt;&lt;P&gt;

\b ensures a word boundary.&lt;P&gt;

(actually in order to play save you should also check for a trailing boundary &lt;C&gt;'t\b&lt;/C&gt;&lt;P&gt;

